Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0021 + 0023-0031 (touches
model_executor/kernels/linear/mxfp8/sm12x_bmm.py, patch 0004's file, only). VLLM_SM12X_BMM_STREAMS=1 (default off):
sm12x_marlin_bmm runs its groups' Marlin MXFP8 GEMMs concurrently at decode sizes (<= 16 tokens): group 0 on the
calling stream, the others on side streams forked from it and joined before the output stack. On GB10 the DSpark
drafter's FP8 wo_a (4 groups a rank at TP=2, [1024, 4096] each, 4.2 MB) ran as four ~25 us GEMMs in a row with a copy
between each, ~108 us a drafter layer, 0.32 ms a round (Oct 21 prose trace): each fills only a few SMs. The same
kernel on the same inputs per group, so the output is bit-identical; the floor is DRAM (16.8 MB a layer, ~67 us).
Larger batches and one-group calls keep the loop. Test: patches/tests/test_sm12x_bmm_streams.py (serve image, GPU:
bit-equal to the loop at 1-16 tokens, eager and in a captured graph).

